The `ctx.setCancellationChecker(null)` call after `rescore()` will not execute if `rescore()` throws an exception (including the `TimeExceededException` that is the primary new path). While this is likely harmless since the `RescoreContext` is not reused after an exception, wrapping the rescore call in a try/finally would make the cleanup deterministic and guard against any future code that might inspect the context after a failed rescore:
```java
try {
    topDocs = ctx.rescorer().rescore(topDocs, context.searcher(), ctx);
} finally {
    ctx.setCancellationChecker(null);
}
```

